<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<component type="desktop-application">
  <id>com.sndcpy.Client</id>
  <name>SNDCPY</name>
    <summary>Mirror and control Android devices over Wi-Fi</summary>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">com.sndcpy.Client.desktop</launchable>
  <developer id="com.github.TheRealRexo">
    <name>Ahmed Elkafasa</name>
  </developer>
  <description>
    <p>SNDCPY mirrors Android devices (video and audio) over Wi-Fi and allows control with a keyboard and mouse. Inspired by scrcpy, it is built from scratch for low-latency, production-grade remote control on a local network.</p>
    <p><b>Features:</b></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Screen mirroring via H.264 (720p/1080p, 30-60 fps)</li>
      <li>Audio forwarding (AAC, Android 10+)</li>
      <li>Remote input: keyboard, mouse, touch gestures</li>
      <li>Secure pairing with ECDH + AES-256-GCM encryption</li>
      <li>mDNS/Bonjour discovery (_sndcpy._tcp.)</li>
      <li>Telemetry (FPS, heap, uptime)</li>
      <li>Cross-platform: Android, iOS, Linux, Windows</li>
    </ul>
    <p>All communication is encrypted with ECDH + AES-256-GCM. Pairing uses one-time 6-digit codes.</p>
  </description>
